From 3e39d6616e9f543070438d22990a7b32bd18521b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 84/90] Mirror connections keep a handler in their pipeline

Mods keep per-connection state on the pipeline's last handler context: Multiloader Data Extensions' known-data-maps reply (pipeline().lastContext().attr(...)) got null from the mirror's empty memory channel, failed every player's configuration and said so in chat. The memory channel now holds a do-nothing handler, as a real connection's packet handler sits there.

UMP 184 mods: the configuration failure is gone (0 log lines, no chat message).
---
 .../dev/horizonlab/platform/HorizonClient.java        | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/horizon-jvm/java/platform/dev/horizonlab/platform/HorizonClient.java b/crates/horizon-jvm/java/platform/dev/horizonlab/platform/HorizonClient.java
index b3db888b83..74becb107b 100644
--- a/crates/horizon-jvm/java/platform/dev/horizonlab/platform/HorizonClient.java
+++ b/crates/horizon-jvm/java/platform/dev/horizonlab/platform/HorizonClient.java
@@ -1121,7 +1121,18 @@ public final class HorizonClient {
         };
         channel.remoteAddress();
         channel.localAddress();
+        // A handler stays in its pipeline, as a real connection's packet handler does: mods keep
+        // per-connection state on the pipeline's last handler context (Multiloader Data
+        // Extensions' known data maps: pipeline().lastContext().attr(...), null on an empty
+        // pipeline, which failed the player's configuration). Netty keeps handlers on a closed
+        // channel's pipeline only until it is deregistered, so it is added after close.
+        // (UMP, 2026-11-15)
         channel.close();
+        try {
+            channel.pipeline().addLast("horizon_packet_handler", new io.netty.channel.ChannelInboundHandlerAdapter());
+        } catch (Throwable t) {
+            Natives.log("Horizon's client: its connection's pipeline has no handler: " + t);
+        }
         try {
             set(net.minecraft.network.Connection.class, connection, "channel", channel);
         } catch (ReflectiveOperationException e) {
